$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1.6 Mechanosynthesis of 4,4’-Stilbenedicarboxylic Acid (3b)
4-Vinylbenzoic acid (3a, 280.3 mg, 2 mmol) was added to a 10 mL Teflon
jar charged with a single stainless steel ball bearing. 150 wt. % NaCl
and a portion of catalyst D (6.0 mg, 0.5 mol %) were added to the jar. 75
µL of ethyl acetate was used as the LAG solvent. The reaction mixture was
then milled for a period of 75 minutes. After each milling period,
another portion of the catalyst was added to the reaction mixture and
milled for another period of time for a total of 5 hours of milling time.
The catalyst and salt were removed from the brown colored crude mixture.
Any remaining brown colored residues and salt, if any, were washed away
with cold acetone and water, and the resulting off-white solid was
filtered and dried in air. Off-white powder (73% yield); 1H-NMR (300 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ 7.48 (s, 2H), δ 7.75 (d, J = 7.92 Hz, 4H), δ 7.94 (d, J = 8.46
Hz, 4H), δ 12.95 (s, 2H) 13C-NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 127.45, δ 130.26, δ
141.50, δ 167.58 HR-MS: calculated for C16H13O4 [M] 269.0808; measure:
269.0813
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition of catalyst, optimized on catalysts, reagents
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mechanochemical Ruthenium-Catalyzed Olefin Metathesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
