$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a stirred solution of compound 5.2 (1eq) in
dry DCM was added 15 mol % Grubbs’ second generation catalyst at room
temperature. The reaction mixture was refluxed for 3 h. The reaction
mixture concentrated in vacuo and purified by flash chromatography. Pure
product 5.3.
(2R,3R,3aS,11S,15aS,E)-11-benzyl-2-(((S)-2,2-dimethyl-1,3-dioxolan-4-yl)methyl)-3-methoxy-2,3,3a,4,10,11,15,15a-octahydrofuro[2,3-i][1,6,3]dioxaazacyclotetradecine-9,12(7H,14H)-dione
(5.3a):
(2R,3R,3aS,11S,15aS,E)-2-(((S)-2,2-dimethyl-1,3-dioxolan-4-yl)methyl)-11-isopropyl-3-methoxy-2,3,3a,4,10,11,15,15a-octahydrofuro[2,3-i][1,6,3]dioxaazacyclotetradecine-9,12(7H,
14H)-dione (5.3c): Purified by flash chromatography using 50% ethyl
acetate in hexane; Yield: 72%. Molecular Formula: C23H37NO8; Rf (50%
ethyl acetate/hexane): 0.3; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 0.95 (d, J =
6.8 Hz, 3H), 1.00 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 1.35 (s, 1H), 1.42 (s, 1H),
1.74-1.80 (m, 1H), 1.86-2.07 (m, 5H), 2.14 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 1H), 2.27-2.34
(d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 3.25 (dd, J = 3.7, 1.9 Hz, 1H), 3.32 (s, 3H),
3.56-3.64 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 3.90-4.00 (m, 4H), 4.03-4.10 (m, 2H),
4.17-4.23 (q, J = 6.4 Hz, 1H), 4.57-4.64 (d, J = 11.6 Hz , 1H), 4.92-5.00
(m, 2H), 5.55-5.65 (m, 1H), 5.75 (ddd, J = 13.6, 7.4, 3.5 Hz, 1H), 1H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 18.2, 19.3, 22.6, 25.6, 27.0, 29.6, 31.8,
33.6, 35.8, 38.9, 48.4, 57.4, 60.8, 61.2, 64.6, 69.7, 74.1, 79.6, 92.2,
108.5, 127.4, 135.8, 156.1, 171.2; LRMS: (ES+) m/z = 456 (M+1), 478
(M+23).
