$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Macrocycles 46.2.1-46.5.1; General Procedure
To a stirred solution of the appropriate diene 46.2-46.5 (85 mg) in
CH2Cl2 (100 mL) was added G-II (10 mol%). The mixture was stirred for 16
h at 40°C until all the material was consumed. It was then concentrated
under reduced pressure, and the residue was purified by column
chromatography (hexanes-EtOAc, 5:5).
(2R,3R,3aS,8S)-8-Benzyl-2-[(benzyloxy)methyl]-3-methoxy-2,3,3a,4,5,8,9,12,15,15a-decahydrofuro[3,2-i][1,6,3]dioxazacyclotetradecine-7,10-dione
(46.2.1)
(2R,3R,3aS,8S)-2-[(Benzyloxy)methyl]-8-sec-butyl-3-methoxy-2,3,3a,4,5,8,9,12,15,15a-decahydrofuro[3,2-i][1,6,3]dioxazacyclotetradecine-7,10-dione
(46.4.1) Colorless oil; yield: 26.4 mg (72%). Molecular formula:
C26H37NO7; Rf = 0.4 (hexanes-EtOAc, 5:5). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
7.36-7.27 (m, 5 H), 3.67 (dd, J = 9.93, 5.31 Hz, 1 H), 3.61 (dd, J =
9.93, 4.79 Hz, 1 H), 5.84 (br s, 1 H), 5.52 (dt, J = 17.20, 9.60 Hz, 1
H), 5.29-5.25 (m, 1 H), 5.15-5.04 (m, 2 H), 4.56-4.53 (m, 4 H), 4.29 (dd,
J = 8.81, 4.86 Hz, 1 H), 4.22-4.16 (m, 1 H), 4.13-4.04 (m, 1 H),
3.49-3.40 (m, 3 H), 2.48-2.35 (m, 2 H), 2.27-2.18 (m, 1 H), 1.92-1.82 (m,
1 H), 1.61-1.49 (m, 5 H), 0.93-0.89 (m, 6 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
= 172.0, 155.8, 137.9, 137.9, 128.4, 128.2, 127.8, 127.8, 118.2, 82.8,
73.4, 71.5, 69.9, 64.6, 63.5, 60.7, 58.3, 43.2, 38.0, 28.8, 24.9, 15.5,
11.6. MS (ES+): m/z = 476.1 [M + 1].
