$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Macrocycles 50a-d; General Procedure G-II (10 mol%) was added to a
stirred solution of the appropriate diene 47.2-47.5 (30 mg) in CH2Cl2
(100 mL), and the mixture was stirred for 16 h at 40°C until the starting
material was completely consumed. The mixture was then concentrated under
reduced pressure and the residue was purified by column chromatography
(hexanes-EtOAc, 5:5).
(1R,5S,13R,14S,15R)-5-Isopropyl-15-methoxy-14-[(phenylsulfonyl)
methyl]-3,8,16-trioxa-6-azabicyclo[11.2.1]hexadec-10-ene-4,7-dione (50a)
Colorless oil; yield: 20.4 mg (72%). Molecular formula: C23H31NO8S; Rf =
0.2 (hexanes-EtOAc, 5:5). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.90 (d, J = 7.47
Hz, 2 H), 7.67-7.62 (m, 1 H), 7.56 (d, J = 7.72 Hz, 2 H), 5.88-5.82, (m,
1 H), 5.75-5.64 (m, 1 H), 5.30-5.22 (m, 1 H), 5.13-5.09 (m, 2 H), 4.57
(br s, 2 H), 4.33-4.19, (m, 3 H), 3.54-3.48 (m, 1 H), 3.42-3.40 (m, 5 H),
3.25-3.19 (m, 2 H), 3.10-3.02 (m, 1 H), 2.20-2.10 (m, 1 H), 0.98 (d, J =
6.80 Hz, 3 H), 0.90 (d, J = 6.56 Hz, 3 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
171.8, 155.9, 140.0, 136.4, 133.6, 129.2, 128.1, 128.0, 118.7, 82.3,
78.9, 64.6, 63.7, 60.5, 59.0, 56.7, 53.4, 40.9, 31.9, 31.1, 29.7, 29.6,
29.3, 22.7. MS (ES+): m/z m/z = 482.3 [M + 1].
