$DATUM RCM product 14{2} A round-bottomed flask was fitted with a magnetic
stirring bar and charged with 4{19} (80mg, 0:24mmol), dry CH2Cl2 (24 mL),
Grubbs II (20 mg, 0:024 mmol) and the mixture was stirred at rt.
overnight. The mixture was concentrated in vacuo, and the residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (EtOAc:heptane 3:1). The title
compound as a brown oil (51mg, 70%). Purity: >95%. RP-HPLC: R t =
4:73min, IR (neat) cm-1: 3234, 3000, 2967, 1649, 1606, 1529, 1401, 1285,
1231, 1048, 1023, 1005, 695; 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 10.42 (s, 1H),
7.66-7.57 (m, 3H), 7.57-7.49 (m, 1H), 7.47-7.38 (m, 2H), 6.59-6.47 (m,
1H), 6.45-6.37 (m, 2H), 6.17 (dd, J = 11:1; 2:1 Hz, 1H), 5.39 (d, J = 5:3
Hz, 1H), 4.87 (d, J = 9:4 Hz, 1H), 4.73-4.60 (m, 1H), 3.07-2.91 (m, 1H),
2.47-2.40 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 166.2, 166.2, 149.6,
143.1, 138.5, 132.4, 131.8, 128.3, 127.6, 126.8, 110.5, 110.4, 73.3,
63.0, 34.1; HRMS (ESI) m/z: calcd for C17H16N2O4 [M+ H]+ 313.1183, found
313.1186.
